Wolfgang Ratzka suggests yet another way to insert a `section-tree' somewhere in

a document and move it around.

I'll be happy with whatever the designers of this section (-: of LaTeX3 come up
with to make this possible in a reasonable way, but...:

Wolfgang (and other people) try to prevent confusion between the old and a new
section command by introducing uppercase letters in the command name.
I agree that new commands should not behave differently from old commands with
the same name. But using uppercase letters in command-names should be confined
(IMHO) to infrequently used, or low-level commands.

Typing a mix of upper- and lowercase characters is very uncomfortable!

